{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Speak to the assembly, saying.</b> He said <b>speak</b> — a term of severity in this matter, for it is actually for their benefit, to save their lives, to convey that HaShem is zealous concerning one who wishes to harm himself by not going up. Therefore the word of the supreme King came to compel him to go up, so that they not destroy themselves, for they are the property of Heaven. And He said the word <b>saying</b> a second time, and it was not sufficient with what He had previously said — <b>and He spoke… saying</b> — because since He employed a term of severity, He thereby made known that this very severity is for the exaltation of the treasured people, that HaShem is zealous over their loss. Further, the word <b>saying</b> intends that there is no obligation to say in this exact expression <b>go up</b> and so forth, but rather in whatever expression the intended meaning — go up and so forth — is conveyed, even if he says it in different words. And therefore you will find that he did not say ״go up״ but rather ״turn aside״ and so forth, and in the place where he should have said ״the dwelling of Korah״ and so forth, he said ״from the tents of these wicked men״."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:23.056834903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}